cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this index, its data or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "fact-provenance: an open index of where web claims come from"
abstract: >-
  A small, searchable index of factual claims taken from public sources, where
  every claim keeps a return address: the page it came from, the sentence around
  it, a digest of that page, when the page was first seen, and — where the page
  cited a source of its own next to that sentence — the URL it cited. Records are
  served as W3C PROV-O over JSON-LD. It does not judge whether a claim is true;
  it makes the claim checkable.
authors:
  - name: "Fact Provenance maintainers"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vimes1984/fact-provenance"
url: "https://factprovenance.org"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
keywords:
  - provenance
  - PROV-O
  - JSON-LD
  - linked-data
  - claim-extraction
  - fact-checking
  - open-data
  - transparency
  - SQLite
  - FTS5
  - Python
type: software
